Local review patch: propagate T6032 cpufreq initialization failure
Base: m1n1 4184923ffb2dff079b384d6a32cc02142aa14572, after 0001..0010
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Keep legacy cpufreq best-effort behavior. For T6032 only, stop the kernel
payload path before secondary startup when cpufreq initialization fails. The
existing HV and proxy caller contracts are unchanged.

--- a/src/payload.c
+++ b/src/payload.c
@@ -316,5 +316,7 @@
     if (kernel && fdt) {
-        cpufreq_init();
+        int cpufreq_status = cpufreq_init();
+        if (chip_id == T6032 && cpufreq_status < 0)
+            return -1;
         if (smp_start_secondaries() < 0)
             return -1;
         mitigations_perform();
